# Shared project notebook

- Read `PROJECT_NOTES.md` before recording project history, decisions or feature implementation details.
- When the user says “add this to notes”, “add this information”, or equivalent wording, append it to the appropriate section of `PROJECT_NOTES.md`.
- When the user says “add this to special”, “add this to special notes”, or equivalent wording, append it to the final `Special Notes` section of `PROJECT_NOTES.md` and keep that section at the end of the file.
- When the user supplies a contributor name, attribute the entry to that name. Otherwise attribute user-requested entries to `Mihirbhati18 (Mihir)`.
- Every entry must include a date, author and accurate status.
- Preserve existing contributor history. Record corrections as new dated entries rather than silently deleting old notes.
- Record implemented features with their purpose, user experience, technology, working logic/data flow, business boundaries, classifications, files, testing, fallbacks, limitations and related pull request.
- Never describe planned work as implemented.
- Never place secrets, tokens, passwords or private customer data in the notebook.
- `MONSOONCOVER_SPEC.md` remains authoritative. Notes cannot override its product or business rules.
